; Regression test for GitHub issue #3320
;
; On an `account` directive line, a semicolon that follows a hard
; separator -- two or more spaces, or a tab -- begins a comment, as it
; ends the payee on a transaction's first line.  The account name ends
; before the separator.  Ledger used to take the whole rest of the line as
; the name, so `account baz  ; bar` declared an account named "baz  ; bar",
; which no posting could use: a posting ends its account name at the
; first hard separator.
;
; A semicolon after a single space, or after no space at all, stays part
; of the name, as it does in a posting, where `foo ; bar` names one
; account.  Nested `account` lines follow the same rule.

account foo ; bar
account baz  ; bar
account tabbed	; after a tab
account spaced 	; after a space and a tab
account bare  ;
account semi;colon  ; only the second semicolon follows a separator
account Parent  ; on the parent
    account Child	; on the nested child

test accounts
Parent
Parent:Child
bare
baz
foo ; bar
semi;colon
spaced
tabbed
end test
